From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenHarmony PC Developer <goblinrs@yeah.net>
Date: Thu, 4 Sep 2026 04:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] guard dlinfo with __GLIBC__

dlinfo() is a glibc-specific extension not available on OHOS libc.
Guard the dlinfo() call with __GLIBC__ so the code compiles on OHOS.
The dlinfo() call is only used in debug trace mode for printing
the driver library path and has no functional impact.

Signed-off-by: OpenHarmony PC Developer <goblinrs@yeah.net>
---
 source/loader/ze_loader.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/source/loader/ze_loader.cpp b/source/loader/ze_loader.cpp
--- a/source/loader/ze_loader.cpp
+++ b/source/loader/ze_loader.cpp
@@ -458,7 +458,7 @@
             {
                 if (debugTraceEnabled) {
                     std::string message = "Loading Driver " + name + " succeeded";
-#ifndef _WIN32
+#if !defined(_WIN32) && defined(__GLIBC__)
                     // TODO: implement same message for windows, move dlinfo to ze_util.h as a macro
                     struct link_map *dlinfo_map;
                     if (dlinfo(handle, RTLD_DI_LINKMAP, &dlinfo_map) == 0) {
--
